          %h2#graphical_criterion_for_validity Graphical criterion for validity
          %p
            In his original Linear Logic paper, Girard gave an interesting purely graphical criterion for a proof structure to be a proof net (i.e., “valid”), based on his so-called “cyclic trips” and “longtrip criterion”. Later this criterion was simplified and improved by Danos and Regnier, who at the same time showed that validity of a proof structure could be decided in polynomial time. We give this criterion below. (
            %strong N.B.
            this criterion as given by them works for proof structures of type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
