              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              is a connected acyclic graph (considered as an unoriented graph, forgetting edge orientations).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              The proof is quite technical, but it is of fundamental importance in the analysis of proof nets. The method is to “sequentialize” a proof structure that satisfies this graphical criterion (i.e., provide a sequent deduction for it). This is by an inductive procedure which first removes consideration of outer par switches (replacing a proof structure of type
